C('6.2.2-01','Which can contribute to background radiation?',('Rocks and cosmic radiation','Both are natural contributors.'),('Only a deliberate classroom source','Background exists without it.'),('A shadow alone','A shadow is not radioactive material.'),('A static ruler mark','It is not the physical radiation source.'))
C('6.2.2-02-M02','What does a G-M counter record?',('Pulses triggered by radiation interactions','Ionisation initiates detection.'),('Every nucleus in the source directly','Only detected events are counted.'),('Only visible colour','That is not its basic signal.'),('The source mass with no calibration','Counting is not direct weighing.'))
C('6.2.3-02-M01','What is alpha radiation?',('Helium nuclei','Two protons and two neutrons.'),('Electrons','That is beta-minus.'),('Photons','That is gamma.'),('Neutral hydrogen atoms','That is not alpha.'))
C('6.2.3-02-M03','Which emission is neutral electromagnetic radiation?',('Gamma','It consists of photons.'),('Alpha','It has positive charge.'),('Beta-minus','It has negative charge.'),('A proton beam','Protons are positively charged.'))
C('6.2.3-01','What is predictable for one unstable nucleus?',('Its decay is random rather than exactly scheduled','Population statistics differ from an individual event.'),('Its exact decay second from its age alone','That is not predictable.'),('It must decay at one half-life','Half-life is a population measure.'),('It cannot decay before one half-life','Events can occur earlier.'))
C('6.2.5-01','After one half-life, what expected fraction remains?',('One half','This defines the interval.'),('None','Decay is not complete then.'),('One quarter','That follows two half-lives.'),('All nuclei','The expected population has fallen.'))
C('6.2.1-01','Which is an exposure-reduction principle?',('Reduce time near the source','Time affects accumulated exposure.'),('Hold the source close to the body','Distance should be increased appropriately.'),('Open a sealed source','Containment should be preserved.'),('Remove controlled storage','Secure storage is part of control.'))
C('6.2.5-02','Background-corrected count rate falls from 120 to 30 counts/s. How many half-lives?',('Two','120 to 60 to 30.'),('One','That leaves 60.'),('Three','That leaves 15.'),('Four','That leaves 7.5.'))
C('6.2.5-02','Total rate is 55 counts/s and background 5 counts/s. What source rate is used?',('50 counts/s','Subtract background.'),('60 counts/s','This adds background.'),('11 counts/s','This divides instead.'),('55 counts/s','This leaves the background included.'))
C('6.2.3-03-M01','With positive plate above and negative below, which way does beta-minus deflect?',('Upward','The negative particle force opposes the downward field.'),('Downward like alpha','Its charge sign is opposite alpha’s.'),('Straight solely because it is neutral','Beta-minus is charged.'),('Only along the beam forever','There is a transverse force.'))
C('6.2.4-01-M02','Alpha emission begins at A = 230, Z = 90. What daughter numbers result?',('A = 226, Z = 88','Remove four nucleons and two protons.'),('A = 230, Z = 91','That is beta-minus change.'),('A = 226, Z = 92','The Z direction is incorrect.'),('A = 234, Z = 92','This adds the emitted alpha.'))
C('6.2.5-02','Half-life is 4 h. What fraction remains after 12 h?',('One eighth','Three halving intervals elapsed.'),('One third','The decrease is not linear in time.'),('One quarter','That is two intervals.'),('Zero','The ideal exponential does not reach zero at that finite time.'))
